    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "This decision turns on POL-NS-24 (Driver no-show). The booking was scheduled for 21:15 (EV-TRIP-05056). POL-NS-21 gives the driver a 300 s free wait, so he had to be at the pickup by 21:20:00. He was not. The trip record's arrival event is empty (arrived_at null, arrived_by_deadline false), and the platform's own arrival check on the GPS trace for this trip — EV-GPS-05056, which is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, 49 fixes, 100% coverage, no gap over 120 s — returns corroborated = false with no fix inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. The trace reports the vehicle at 0 kph on every fix from 21:09:30 through the 21:23:00 fix, i.e. stationary for the last stretch of the booking until the rider cancelled at 21:23:15. So the driver never came within the arrival radius. Under POL-NS-24 the rider was entitled to cancel at no charge, and the 5.00 SGD fee on the ledger (EV-FARE-05056, total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is refunded in full — the whole contested 5.00 SGD.\n\nThe driver's answer, 'I was coming', is not borne out: the only machine record of his movement shows a stationary car, and the arrival check records no arrival. He also made no contact. The chat log (EV-CHAT-05056) carries two messages, both sent by the rider (21:16:40 and 21:19:30), and the only call in the record is the rider's own, placed at 21:20:10, which rang 30 s unanswered. Because the driver both missed the 21:20:00 deadline and failed to attempt contact, POL-NS-24 also gives the rider a 5.00 SGD goodwill credit; per POL-GEN-03 that is recorded as a referral, it neither suppresses nor replaces the refund, and it is listed above.\n\nNothing is owed to the driver. POL-NS-22 attaches the 5.00 SGD fee to the driver only where the driver cancels after the free wait; here the driver never cancelled at all and the free wait never started, so the fee rests on no condition the policy recognises and there is no compensation for time or fuel on a trip he never reached. The driver's request for NO_ACTION and his conditional request for DRIVER_COMPENSATION both fail for that reason.\n\nOn the rider's POL-NS-23 point: the contact failure is real and the record's contact_before_cancel block reports obligation_met false, but POL-NS-23 is triggered by a driver no-show cancellation, which did not happen here. It reinforces the rider's position; the refund itself follows from POL-NS-24.\n\nI do not escalate. The driver argued the question of arrival is open (POL-GEN-26) because arrived_at is empty. It is not open: a complete, unimpaired GPS trace covers the whole window and shows where the car was, so the record establishes that he did not arrive. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05056-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact, and traffic could not explain a stationary vehicle in any event; the rider's 'petrol station' detail is not in the record either. Neither point changes the result.\n\nThe rider's repeat no-show concern under POL-NS-25 does not fire: the profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d counter, and this fee does not stand in any case.\n\nConfidence is 0.90. Every artifact that carries a deciding fact — the trip record, the GPS trace and the chat log — has weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; and this dispute is worth 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's first band, where POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final.",
    "referrals_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
